# claude: what the release archives leave out.
#
# export-ignore tells `git archive` to leave a path out of the archives
# it makes. GitHub makes its archive of a tag with `git archive`
# (https://github.com/aryx/ocaml-elm-playground/archive/refs/tags/<tag>.tar.gz),
# and that archive is what the opam packages' url points at (see
# 0.2.1's opam files, made by `opam publish`): every package of the
# release -- tiny_libs as well as tinybox -- downloads the same archive,
# so whatever is in it, every user downloads.
#
# docs/ is the GitHub Pages site: the examples, games and apps built
# for the web, the generated API docs (make website), the notes of
# docs/claude_notes/, the two toy example projects of the README. No
# package builds or tests anything from it (no dune rule reads docs/),
# so it stays in the repository and on the website, and out of the
# archives: 30 MB of 131 uncompressed, the archive going from 73 MB
# to 64 MB compressed (September 2026).
#
# What must stay, although large: the golden frames (tests/2d/golden,
# tests/3d/golden, 50 MB), which tinybox embeds as its menu's
# thumbnails at build time.
#
# To see what an archive would hold, without making a release:
#   git archive HEAD | tar -t | less
# (with uncommitted changes to this file, add --worktree-attributes).
#
# Caveat: `dune-release distrib` makes its own archive from a clone of
# the repository, and may not honour export-ignore; check its archive
# before publishing one made that way.
docs/ export-ignore
